content.text:
Now game.js. Let me write it fully.

Key functions and flow. I need to be careful with `state.notes` and localStorage.

Let me define DOM cache after DOM load. Since script is module at end of body, DOM is ready.

Pseudo:

```js
import { STORY, ACTS, NOTES, SURVIVORS, LOST } from './story.js';

const SAVE_KEY = 'stillalive.save.v2';
const NOTES_KEY = 'stillalive.notes.v1';
const SOUND_KEY = 'stillalive.sound.v1';

const $ = (sel, root=document) => root.querySelector(sel);
const $$ = ...

const els = { ... };

let state = null;
let currentChoices = [];
let busy = false;
let chapterTimer = null, chapterDone = null;
let toastTimer = null;
let pendingNote = null;
let calloutNoteId = null;
let lastFocus = null;
let drawerOpen = false;
let confirmOpen = false;
let soundOn = false;
let soundPref = false;
let audio = null;
let snowRaf = null;
let reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
```

Helpers:
```js
const clamp = (n,min,max)=>Math.max(min,Math.min(max,n));
const pad = n=>String(n).padStart(2,'0');
function escapeHtml? not needed if using textContent.
function setText(el, text){ el.textContent = text; }
function show(el){ el.hidden=false; }
function hide(el){ el.hidden=true; }
```

Storage:
```js
function readJSON(key, fallback) { try { const raw=localStorage.getItem(key); return raw?JSON.parse(raw):fallback; } catch { return fallback; } }
function writeJSON(key,val) { try { localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(val)); } catch {} }
function readNotes(){ const arr=readJSON(NOTES_KEY, []); return Array.isArray(arr)?arr.filter(id=>NOTES[id]):[]; }
function persistNotes(){ writeJSON(NOTES_KEY, state.notes); }
```

newState:
```js
function newState() {
  return {
    version: 2,
    nodeId: STORY.start,
    act: 0,
    day: 0,
    date: '12 October 1972',
    location: 'Montevideo, Uruguay',
    altitude: 'Sea level',
    alive: 45,
    stats: { warmth: 55, strength: 60, hope: 55 },
    food: 3,
    showFood: false,
    third: 'Tintín',
    flags: {},
    inventory: ['A boarding pass'],
    notes: readNotes(),
    visited: [],
    checkpoint: null,
    echo: null,
    startedAt: Date.now(),
    completed: false,
  };
}
```
`act:0` means no act card until first goTo. Good.

Checkpoint snapshot:
```js
function snapshot(s) {
  const copy = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(s));
  delete copy.checkpoint;
  delete copy.echo;
  return copy;
}
```
When saving checkpoint, current nodeId is the current node. Good.

Save:
```js
function save() { if (state) writeJSON(SAVE_KEY, state); }
```
On note changes, persist notes separately.

`hasSave`: read and validate.

Screen management:
```js
function showScreen(name) {
  const map = { title: els.screenTitle, game: els.screenGame, ending: els.screenEnding, death: els.screenDeath };
  for (const [k,el] of Object.entries(map)) el.hidden = k !== name;
  document.body.dataset.screen = name;
  if (name === 'game') { els.screenGame.hidden=false; }
}
```
When showing game, don't reset. On title, update continue button.

`startNew()`:
```js
function startNew() {
  stopChapter();
  state = newState();
  state.notes = readNotes();
  save();
  showScreen('game');
  els.drawer... close if open
  goTo(STORY.start, { chapter: true });
  if (soundPref) setSound(true, {silentLabel:true});
  document.title = 'STILL ALIVE — A True Story of the Andes';
  updateSoundButton();
}
```
But `goTo` unlocks flight note, which is already in global notes on replay; no callout. Fine.

Start button handler:
```js
function handleStart() {
  if (hasSave()) { openConfirm('new'); } else startNew();
}
```
Confirm modal context: `confirmMode = 'new' | 'restart' | 'title'`. `openConfirm(mode)`. Title text changes:
- new: "Start a new story?" "You have a saved story on the mountain. Starting over will replace it."
- restart: "Start the story over?" "Your current progress will be lost. The field notes you have recovered will be kept."
- title: "Return to the title screen?" "Your progress is saved. You can continue later."
- If mode title, the yes button label "Return to title" and no wipe. But returning to title doesn't lose progress. Let's implement:
  - `confirmMode='title'` → yes → showTitle() (save persists).
  - `new`/`restart` → yes → startNew().
Modal copy dynamic.

But the brand link: if a game is in progress, returning to title is safe. Use confirm? It's a minor action; maybe just go title. If the user clicks brand, likely wants title. Do it directly: `showTitle()`. No confirm. Simpler. The confirm modal only for restart/new.
- Restart from topbar: openConfirm('restart').
- Death "Start over": startNew() directly? It wipes. It's already over; fine. Or confirm. Direct.
- Ending "Walk it again": startNew() direct.

`showTitle()`:
- showScreen('title'); updateContinueButton(); stopChapter(); closeDrawer();
- document.title = main.
- Maybe scroll top.
- Keep state in memory? If a game is ongoing and you return to title, state remains. Continue loads from save. Fine.
- `btn-continue` label with save day.

`continueGame()`:
- const s = readSave(); if (!s) return;
- state = s; ensure fields exist (migrate/default).
- state.notes = merge with global notes? If global notes has more, add. `state.notes = Array.from(new Set([...(state.notes||[]), ...readNotes()]))`. Good.
- showScreen('game');
- if (state.completed) … maybe node ending; 
- const node = STORY.nodes[state.nodeId];
- if node.kind === 'ending' → renderEnding(node);
- else if node.kind === 'death' → renderDeath(node);
- else goTo(state.nodeId, { chapter: false, scroll: false });
- If soundPref, setSound.
- `renderNode` will not show chapter card.
- Need to avoid `goTo` resetting act etc. It will set from node.

`updateContinueButton()`:
```js
const s = readSave();
if (s && STORY.nodes[s.nodeId]) {
  els.btnContinue.hidden = false;
  const day = s.nodeId === STORY.start ? 'the beginning' : `Day ${s.day ?? '?'}`;
  els.btnContinue.textContent = `Continue · ${day}`;
} else hidden = true;
```

`readSave()` validate version 2 and node exists; ensure stats/numbers. If older, delete? Just return null.

`goTo(id, opts={})`:
- node valid.
- `const prevAct = state.act;`
- `state.act = node.act ?? state.act;`
- copy fields. For `showFood`, if node.showFood !== undefined set; else if node.act < 3 set false? Keep.
- `state.alive = node.alive != null ? node.alive : state.alive;`
- inventory.
- `state.nodeId=id;`
- if note: `const newly = unlockNote(node.note); pendingNote = newly ? node.note : null;`
- visited.
- `state.echo` remains until render.
- save.
- if node.kind === 'ending' → renderEnding.
- death → renderDeath.
- else if opts.chapter !== false && node.act !== prevAct && ACTS[node.act] → showChapter(node.act, ()=>renderNode(node, opts)).
  - Need to handle the first start: prevAct 0 → card. Good.
  - On act change, card.
- else renderNode.
- Note: `unlockNote` might call `updateHUD` before game screen? fine.
- `pendingNote` is global; if chapter card delays render, keep. If another goTo occurs? no.

`renderNode(node, opts={})`:
- `showScreen('game')` (if not already).
- Set scene act, title.
- prose render.
- echo:
  - remove existing echo.
  - if state.echo: create div, textContent = template(state.echo), insert after prose. Set state.echo=null. save later.
- callout:
  - if pendingNote: show with title; set calloutNoteId; else hide.
  - pendingNote=null.
- choices.
- updateHUD.
- footer.
- focus title.
- scroll stage into view if opts.scroll !== false and state.visited length > 1? Use `if (window.scrollY > 10) setTimeout(()=>els.stage.scrollIntoView({behavior: reducedMotion?'auto':'smooth', block:'start'}), 30);`
  - But on mobile, HUD is above; scrolling to stage is good.
- save (after echo cleared? state.echo set to null; save).
- document.title = `${node.title} · Still Alive`.
- If node is ending/death, handled earlier, not here.

`renderProse(container, paragraphs)`:
- clear.
- filter.
- for each, p = document.createElement('p'); class if p.class; textContent = template(p.text). For strings, template(p).
- set animation delay. If container is ending, no need but fine.
- For paragraph objects with `class: 'letter'`, first-letter CSS overridden. Good.
- Important: The long Spanish letter contains quotes and em dashes; textContent fine.
- `template(str)` replaces `{{third}}` globally.
- Some paragraphs are conditional objects with `if` and `unless`. Implement:
```js
function paragraphVisible(p) {
  if (typeof p === 'string') return true;
  if (p.if && !state.flags[p.if]) return false;
  if (p.unless && state.flags[p.unless]) return false;
  return true;
}
```

`renderChoices(node)`:
- clear; currentChoices = [];
- filter by choice.if/unless.
- for each:
  - required check: `choice.requires` e.g. {stat:'hope', min:20, text:'...'} → locked. Add hint.
  - button.
  - class.
  - num label = currentChoices.length + 1.
  - for continue no num.
  - body span; text span; hint span if locked/hint.
  - arrow.
  - add event.
  - style animation delay = `${i*55}ms`.
- If no choices: maybe add a continue button to restart? Not for ending. For safety, add "Continue" to ending? No.

`choose(index)`:
- if busy, state null, not game screen.
- choice = currentChoices[index]; if !choice or locked.
- busy = true.
- `state.checkpoint = snapshot(state);` (before effects)
- `state.echo = choice.text;` (template at render)
- apply effects; set flags; third.
- updateHUD.
- click sound.
- mark picked; disable others.
- setTimeout 360:
  - death checks:
    - if strength <=0 || warmth <=0 → goTo('death_exposure').
    - else if food <=0 && strength <=8 && state.act>=4 → goTo('death_starvation').
    - else goTo(resolveNext(choice.next)); 
  - busy=false after.
- Note: If a choice's `next` is an object with ifStat, check after effects. Good.
- If the choice has `requires` and is locked, no click.
- Some choices might have `set` flags used by conditional text.
- `state.checkpoint` saved with save() in goTo. Good.
- If death from stats, the death screen uses `state.checkpoint` persisted in state. Good.
- Important: `goTo` calls save() before render; checkpoint included. Fine.
- If the death is triggered by a choice leading to `death_fall`, goTo handles kind death. Good.
- If a choice is "Continue" and it leads to a node, echo "Continue" would appear; exclude echo for continue kind. Set `state.echo = choice.kind === 'continue' ? null : choice.text;`
- `busy = false` should be set after screen render; use 500ms. For chapter transitions, the overlay is up to 2s; busy would remain true and block keyboard. That's fine; but set busy false before chapter callback? If chapter, choices aren't rendered for 2s. Keyboard shouldn't work. Keep busy true until render? Hmm. Simpler: set `busy=false` after 400ms regardless; the chapter overlay blocks clicks but keyboard digits could trigger choices on the old node. Since currentChoices still old, a keypress would choose again! Need to guard. Set `currentChoices=[]` immediately after selecting? But then the chosen button event... We can set a `transitioning` flag true and only clear after render. Use `busy` true until the new node is rendered. In goTo→renderNode, set busy=false at the end. For death/ending, set busy=false. And chapter card: render after; set false. This is clean.
  - On choose: busy=true. After 420ms call goTo; goTo/renderNode sets busy=false. If chapter is shown, busy remains true until callback. Good.
  - Disable all buttons immediately.
  - If goTo fails, set busy=false.
- On keyboard, if busy return.

`resolveNext(next)`:
```js
if (typeof next === 'string') return next;
if (!next) return null;
if (next.ifStat) return (state.stats[next.ifStat] ?? 0) >= next.min ? next.then : next.otherwise;
if (next.ifFlag) return state.flags[next.ifFlag] ? next.then : next.otherwise;
return next.otherwise || next.then;
```

`applyEffects(effects)`:
- if no effects return [].
- for stats, clamp.
- for food clamp >=0.
- return deltas; show.
- `state.showFood` may be set by node; food hidden before.
- Delats display labels.
- If warmth/strength low, HUD pulses (CSS). Good.

`showDeltas`:
- remove existing `.delta-float`.
- create; append spans; text like "+4 Hope" or "−3 Strength" (use proper minus). For food: "+1 Ration" or "−1 Ration".
- stage append. Remove after 2100ms.
- If no deltas, maybe show nothing.
- The deltas are relative to actual change; if clamped, show actual. If effect 5 but stat at 98 → +2. Good.
- Use `delta.is-up` or down.

`updateHUD()`:
- set day label: state.day === 0 ? "Day 0" : `Day ${state.day}`; maybe pad to 2 digits? Keep "Day 4". The design looks better with "DAY 04". Use `Day ${pad(state.day)}` for numbers <100. But chapter card shows Day 0. Let's do `Day ${state.day}`. Hmm. The big number style 2.25rem. "Day 60" fits. Use no pad. 
- date.
- location, altitude.
- stats: numbers, bar width; low class if <=25.
- alive number, pips.
- food: hidden class if !state.showFood; value; bar width = clamp(food/4*100, 0,100); label "3 days" update. Need `#food-stat` and `#stat-food`. The structure has `<span id="stat-food">3</span> days`. Change to `el.statFood.textContent = state.food;`.
- inventory: clear, add li for each. If empty, "Nothing but the clothes on your back".
- note count.
- act progress: set text `Act ${roman} of V`; fill width. `chapter-count` = ACTS[act].title maybe. The footer currently has chapter-count. Set to node.date? state.date. Use `state.date`.
- Pips: build 45 spans once; update `.is-lost` for i >= alive. The order: first alive light, rest lost. Good.
- If alive < 0, clamp.
- Stat bar widths use style.width = `${value}%`.
- Add `aria-valuenow`? The stat track could have role progressbar. Not in HTML. Could set attribute on `.stat-track` but no role. Minor. Add `aria-label` to stat? Not necessary.

`unlockNote(id)`:
- if !NOTES[id] return false.
- if state.notes includes id return false.
- push.
- persistNotes.
- update note count.
- toast(`Field note recovered · ${NOTES[id].title}`) unless drawer open.
- return true.
- Note: On new game, state.notes = readNotes() so previously unlocked notes are already there. Fine.

`renderNotes()`:
- progress.
- clear list.
- order notes by `index` from NOTES values.
- for each note:
  - unlocked = state.notes.includes(id)
  - div class note + locked id
  - head: index (01,02), title (unlocked ? note.title : "Unrecovered field note")
  - body (unlocked ? note.body : "")
  - source (unlocked ? note.source : "")
- Add data-note id.
- Drawer foot static.
- If all collected, progress "All 10 recovered" maybe.
- Note count in HUD.

